A final boundary review surfaced one Python-specific edge case worth hardening: direct comparison of two datetimes sharing the same timezone object can use wall-clock ordering during the repeated hour when DST ends. I’m changing the pre-delivery check to compare UTC instants and adding a regression test for the ambiguous hour.
